{"conversation_id":"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Round-3 independent second-architect review of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) has been written to [1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\nAPPROVE WITH CHANGES\n\n### Findings Summary\n\n| ID | Severity | Section | Summary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `MAJOR-1` | MAJOR | §1.1, §3.2, §4.1.1, §5, §6 | Explicitly require the Rust native service to implement [`debruijn-code/encode-scalar`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc#L410-L465) + [`rcode/register-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L262-L271) and [`dao.jing.cbor/encode`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L1-L28) + [`jing/content-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L160-L179) alongside the §4.1.1 ABI binary codec so `:hash` (`R`), `:owner` ([`values/owner-tag`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L123-L130)), `:seal` ([`engine/seal-of`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L299-L302)), `:yin.k/profile` ([`vm/primitive-profile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L338-L356)), and `:address` ([`module.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L92)) match CLJS bit-for-bit. |\n| `MAJOR-2` | MAJOR | §1.1, §4.1.1, §6 W0 | Specify in §4.1.1 that (1) map keys and set elements sort by canonical encoded value bytes (never by `tag 13` arena-reference bytes), (2) `tag 4` (`float64`) canonicalizes NaNs to `0x7ff8000000000000` ([`debruijn_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc#L232-L234), [`cbor.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L19-L20)) and preserves integral floats / `-0.0` on CLJS via `dao.jing.cbor`'s float64 carrier and [`integer-host/exact-integer?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc#L61-L66), and (3) string (`tag 5`) and collection (`tags 8..11`) payloads have a single unambiguous framing rule. |\n| `MINOR-1` | MINOR | §4.1.1, §5, §6 W3–W4 | Specify a deterministic map-traversal order for [`engine/encoder`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L918-L922), [`engine/encode-store`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1044-L1046), [`engine/markers`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L978-L983) / [`lower-resources`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1017-L1028) / [`receive-module`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1110-L1112), [`module/module-entries`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L100-L110) / [`list-modules`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L166-L169), and [`engine/resume-from-run-queue`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2304-L2306) so CLJS and Rust mint identical `:yin.k/c-N` and `:stream-N` IDs. |\n| `MINOR-2` | MINOR | §4.1.1, §6 W0, W3, W4 | Move `NEED_SPACE` + `fetch-response` / `BAD_MESSAGE` / `ABI_MISMATCH` / `RESOURCE_LIMIT` transport tests into W0 and W3 (for effectful once-only retry), and add the Wasmer W1–W4 suite pass and native↔CLJS module-slice parity to W4's `Acceptance:` paragraph. |\n\n### Properties Passing Review\n1. **R2 Body Integrity**: All Round-2 approved sections — all 23 opcode lowerings in §2.3 ([`debruijn_register_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L70-L151), [`register.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L624-L823)), §1.2.1 map↔memory synchronization, §2.4 host-function effect completion ([`run-call-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L564-L580)), §3.1–3.2 continuation payload and restore ([`register-restore`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L403-L450), [`write-back`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L452-L469), [`return-transition`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L492-L518)), §4.2–4.3 stream/custody/FFI two-step ([`ffi-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L583-L617)), and the Round-1 response table — are retained unchanged without silent edits.\n2. **Core-Wasm-1.0 Feature Profile \u0026 WasmGC Non-Goal**: The baseline profile (`i32`/`i64`/`f32`/`f64`, structured control, one non-shared `wasm32` memory, one `call_indirect` table, mutable globals, active segments) is consistent throughout, avoids guest `table.grow`/`table.set`/`memory.copy`/`return_call` instructions, and rightly keeps WasmGC and `externref` as non-goals.\n3. **Import ABI Framing \u0026 `NEED_SPACE` Idempotence**: The `yin.register.host.v1` control-block layout (bytes `0..255`), single `exchange(control_ptr: i32) -\u003e i32` import signature, and sequence-retained `NEED_SPACE` / `fetch-response` protocol cleanly decouple wasm execution from JS/browser assumptions and prevent duplicate effect execution on response buffer growth.\n4. **Toolchain Pins \u0026 Multi-Runtime Differential Harness**: W0 pins match the repository's [mise.toml](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/mise.toml#L6-L7) and [deps.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/deps.edn#L40) versions and require identical wasm binaries to execute with full step and ABI trace comparison across Node and Wasmtime from W1 and Wasmer through W4–W6.\n","duration_seconds":2791.112352,"num_turns":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":1069082,"output_tokens":93852,"thinking_tokens":44593,"cache_read_tokens":4572402,"total_tokens":1162934}}
